I've written the control.py, and state.py scripts to be able to use the RPC3 outlets with homekit and the home app.
There were some challenges with number of telnet sessions that the RPC3 unit allows at a time. It only allows 4 telnet sessions at a time.
The scripts attempt to mitigage homebridge state requests for status by using a cache status file. 
The first request for status will update the status file.
My RPC 3 unit is set to not ask for username or password. 
When configured like this the scripts should work as is.

More info on the Baytech RPC3 
http://www.copyerror.com/2014/04/25/baytech-rpc3-remote-power-controller/
https://www.servethehome.com/baytech-rpc3-deal-remote-switched-8port-pdu-50-windows-app/

This script requires pexpect
https://github.com/pexpect/pexpect
Install using pip:
pip install pexpect
